#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:88
msgid "waitUntilFree(port [, retryTimeMs] [, timeOutMs])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:89
msgid ""
"Returns a deferred promise and fulfills it only when the localhost socket"
" is free.  Will retry on an interval specified in retryTimeMs until the "
"timeout. If not defined the retryTime is 200 ms and the timeout is 2000 "
"ms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:95
msgid ""
"**Number|Object** *port* a valid TCP port number. If an object must "
"contain all the parameters as properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:97
#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:116
#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:133
#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:151
#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:171
msgid ""
"**Number** *[retryTimeMs]* the retry interval in milliseconds - defaultis"
" is 100ms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:98
#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:117
#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:134
#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:152
#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:172
msgid ""
"**Number** *[timeOutMs]* the amount of time to wait until port is free. "
"Default 300ms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:105
msgid "waitUntilFreeOnHost(port [, host] [, retryTimeMs] [, timeOutMs])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:106
msgid ""
"Returns a deferred promise and fulfills it only when the localhost socket"
" is free.  Will retry on an interval specified in retryTimeMs until the "
"timeout. If not defined the retryTime is 200 ms and the timeout is 2000 "
"ms. If the host is not defined, the modules uses the default '127.0.0.1'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:113
#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:131
#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:148
msgid ""
"**Number|Object** *port* a valid TCP port number. If an object, must "
"contain all the parameters as properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:123
msgid "waitUntilUsed(port [, retryTimeMs] [, timeOutMs])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:124
msgid ""
"Returns a deferred promise and fulfills it only when the socket is "
"accepting connections. Will retry on an interval specified in retryTimeMs"
" until the timeout. If the host is not defined the retryTime is 200 ms "
"and the timeout is 2000 ms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:140
msgid "waitUntilUsedOnHost(port [, host] [, retryTimeMs] [, timeOutMs])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:141
msgid ""
"Returns a deferred promise and fulfills it only when the socket is "
"accepting connections. Will retry on an interval specified in retryTimeMs"
" until the timeout. If not defined the retryTime is 200 ms and the "
"timeout is 2000 ms. If the host is not defined the module uses the "
"default '127.0.0.1'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:158
msgid "waitForStatus(port, host, status [, retryTimeMs] [, timeOutMs])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:159
msgid ""
"Waits until the port on host matches the boolean status in terms of use. "
"If the status is true, the promise defers until the port is in use. If "
"the status is false the promise defers until the port is free. If the "
"host is undefined or null, the module uses the default '127.0.0.1'. Also,"
" if not defined the retryTime is 200 ms and the timeout is 2000 ms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:167
msgid ""
"**Number** *port* a valid TCP port number. If an object, must contain all"
" the parameters as properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tcp-port-used_README.md:170
msgid ""
"**Boolean** *status* A boolean describing the condition to wait for in "
"terms of \"in use.\" True indicates wait until the port is in use. False "
"indicates wait until the port is free."
msgstr ""

